---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const contentHtml = `
<p><strong>Kiln 1.1.1 is out.</strong> This release tightens the loop between your AI agent and your 3D printer &mdash; cheaper status signals while a print is running, better failure detection on Pro, an install-doctor that fixes its own broken paths after a Python reinstall, and a handful of quality fixes across the agent surface and the web app at <a href="https://kiln3d.com">kiln3d.com</a>.</p>

<h2>Cheaper signals from your print camera</h2>

<p>Kiln&rsquo;s print monitoring has been camera-aware for a while &mdash; your AI agent could already subscribe to live updates from the printer&rsquo;s camera. The catch was that every notification carried a full snapshot image in its payload, even when the agent only needed to know the camera was working.</p>

<p><strong>1.1.1 splits this into two events.</strong> A lightweight one carries just signals and a path to the latest snapshot (subscribe to this for &ldquo;is the camera seeing my print?&rdquo;). A heavier one carries the full image data (subscribe to this when an agent is actually doing visual reasoning on the frame). Agents pick the one matching their job, and the watcher warns once when the heavy event has a subscriber so the bandwidth cost doesn&rsquo;t sneak up on you.</p>

<h2>Better in-print failure detection (Pro)</h2>

<p>Pro tier now catches common print failures earlier. The detector watches your camera feed for two trouble signatures &mdash; spaghetti / filament tangle (when the printer says it&rsquo;s moving but the camera shows no progress) and stalled prints (when the frame stops changing entirely) &mdash; so your agent can act before a print is ruined. Sensitivity is tunable so you can dial it in for your printer setup.</p>

<h2><code>kiln health</code> now fixes its own broken paths</h2>

<p>A common &ldquo;Kiln stopped working&rdquo; problem is <strong>&ldquo;I reinstalled Python and now Claude Desktop / Claude Code / Codex can&rsquo;t find Kiln anymore.&rdquo;</strong> That&rsquo;s a real path mismatch &mdash; the AI client&rsquo;s config still points at the old Python install, where <code>kiln</code> no longer lives.</p>

<p>Now you don&rsquo;t have to fix it yourself. Just tell your AI agent that Kiln isn&rsquo;t working and it&rsquo;ll diagnose and repair the path mismatch for you &mdash; no manual config editing required.</p>

<h2>Also in 1.1.1</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Wait-on-event for agents</strong> &mdash; instead of polling print status in a loop, an agent can now block until a specific event fires (&ldquo;tell me when the first layer finishes&rdquo;).</li>
  <li><strong>Per-design visibility (Pro)</strong> &mdash; in the Kiln web app at <a href="https://kiln3d.com">kiln3d.com</a>, Pro users can now flip any design between private and shared from the timeline header. Shared designs get a copy-link button.</li>
  <li><strong>A build plate that looks like your build plate</strong> &mdash; the 3D model viewer at <a href="https://kiln3d.com">kiln3d.com</a> now draws rectangle-aware plates from a printer-aware registry. Your model sits on a plate that matches your actual printer&rsquo;s bed, not a generic square.</li>
  <li><strong>Friendlier paywall messages</strong> &mdash; when an agent hits a Pro or Business feature, the message now leads with the feature you asked for, says what the upgrade gets you, and offers both an upgrade path and a &ldquo;do it the free way&rdquo; path. No more cryptic &ldquo;upgrade required&rdquo; dead ends.</li>
  <li><strong>Bambu camera capability</strong> &mdash; the adapter reports camera support correctly even when <code>ffmpeg</code> isn&rsquo;t installed on your computer.</li>
  <li><strong>Cleaner shutdown</strong> &mdash; <code>kiln serve</code> exits the moment its AI client disconnects instead of lingering as a zombie process.</li>
  <li><strong>Stall warnings actually arrive</strong> &mdash; internal print-stall events were getting dropped before they reached subscribers. Fixed.</li>
</ul>

<p>Full release notes: <a href="https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">CHANGELOG.md</a>.</p>

<h2>Upgrading</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Already running Kiln?</strong> Run <code>pip install --upgrade kiln3d</code> and you&rsquo;re on 1.1.1.</li>
  <li><strong>New to Kiln?</strong> Run <code>pip install kiln3d</code>, then follow the <a href="/install">install guide</a> to connect it to your AI client (Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Codex, or any other MCP-compatible client).</li>
</ul>

<p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;"><a href="/install" class="btn">Get Kiln &rarr;</a></p>
`;
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title="Kiln 1.1.1: tighter feedback loop"
  description="Cheaper status signals from your printer to the AI agent running it, better in-print failure detection on Pro, a kiln health command that fixes its own broken paths after a Python reinstall, and a handful of polish fixes across the agent and web surfaces."
  date="May 13, 2026"
  tags={["release", "v1.1.1", "vision", "kiln-health", "polish"]}
>
  <Fragment set:html={contentHtml} />
</BlogPostLayout>
